%I A401624 #17 Nov 09 2026 15:20:08
%S A401624 3,8,35,189,1166,7752,56157,423521,3306171,26571998,218134071,
%T A401624 1822880701,15462635138,132822560771,1153300861300
%N A401624 Number of primes p < 10^n such 2*p-1 is also prime.
%C A401624 Also number of Cunningham chains (second kind) of length two starting before 10^n.
%H A401624 Chris K. Caldwell, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.04483">An Amazing Prime Heuristic</a>, arXiv:2103.04483 [math.HO], 2021. See Table 7.
%H A401624 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/CunninghamChain.html">Cunningham Chain</a>.
%e A401624 p up to 10 are 2 (since 3 is prime), 3 (since 5 is prime), 7 (since 13 is prime) so a(1) = 3.
%t A401624 Table[Length[Select[Prime /@ Range[PrimePi[10^n]], PrimeQ[2 # - 1] &]], {n, 1, 7}]
%o A401624 (PARI) vector(6, m, #select(p -> isprime(2*p - 1), primes([2, 10^m])))
%Y A401624 Cf. A005382, A005383, A092816.
%K A401624 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A401624 1,1
%A A401624 _Henri Lifchitz_, Oct 31 2026
